  "advice_en": "Near term, gold is still pinned down by a 5.1% 10-year yield, and there's no reversal signal yet – but price is sitting on the $4,100–$4,150 base.\nThis isn't the place to dump metal, and it isn't the place to go all in either.\nIf you need to buy, split it into three pieces. Buy the first piece around here.\nHold the second for a dip to $4,040–$4,100.\nBuy the third only on a daily close above $4,200–$4,235 – that's when the trend actually turns.\nA daily close below $4,037 means stop adding and wait for a new base.\nMind the dealer premium and the bid/ask spread on bars and coins: money you'll need within a few months doesn't belong in physical gold.\nBuying to hold for years is fine – just don't chase the intraday pops.",
